# A pipe flange: a bolted disk with a hub, six ribs, a keyed bore,
# six bolt holes and a cross-drilled pin hole.
# Cylinders stand on the Z axis, centred on the origin; rotate turns
# about the origin, so "rotate x z 60" walks a part around the axis.
# Repeated features (ribs, bolts) are gathered into one solid first and
# applied with a single boolean, the way a CAD user would pattern them.

# The disk and the hub (disk: z -5..5, hub: z -5..35)
cylinder flange 40 10 64
cylinder hub 22 40 64
translate hub 0 0 15
union part flange hub

# The bore, right through, and a keyway cut into its side
cylinder bore 14 80 64
difference part part bore
box key 6 6 80
translate key 14 0 15
difference part part key

# Six ribs between the hub and the rim, at 30, 90, 150, ... degrees
box rib 20 4 20
translate rib 28 0 14
rotate rib z 30
copy ribs rib
rotate rib z 60
union ribs ribs rib
rotate rib z 60
union ribs ribs rib
rotate rib z 60
union ribs ribs rib
rotate rib z 60
union ribs ribs rib
rotate rib z 60
union ribs ribs rib
union part part ribs

# Six bolt holes on a 30 mm circle, between the ribs
cylinder bolt 4 20 24
translate bolt 30 0 0
copy bolts bolt
rotate bolt z 60
union bolts bolts bolt
rotate bolt z 60
union bolts bolts bolt
rotate bolt z 60
union bolts bolts bolt
rotate bolt z 60
union bolts bolts bolt
rotate bolt z 60
union bolts bolts bolt
difference part part bolts

# A pin hole drilled across the hub, through the bore and the keyway
cylinder pin 5 60 32
rotate pin y 90
translate pin 0 0 25
difference part part pin
